 " gives all of them."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"370200c6-8634-4e1d-993f-19e6d3ec5744"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A continuous section ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " picks a total vertex ",
 StyleBox["s(p)", "TI"],
 " over every base vertex ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ", with ",
 StyleBox["{s(p), s(q)}", "TI"],
 " a total edge for every base edge ",
 StyleBox["{p, q}", "TI"],
 ". The results are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSection"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSection", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ee65050e-dd44-43b5-af8f-8bb33c09a716"],
 " objects."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"42a56470-230d-4375-90d2-bb10f7f0d2a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The sections come in a fixed order, the same on every call. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["FindInfraSection"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraSection", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["fib", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25088db0-9e0c-458f-b915-43a52c188925"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["RandomInfraSection"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraSection", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["fib", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     ButtonBox["Properties",
      BaseStyle->"Link"], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "\"\<Continuous\>\"", "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<NextVertexFunction\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     ButtonBox["Identity",
      BaseStyle->"Link"]}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e84fb0e8-c455-4915-8b05-46f602e93952"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RandomInfraSection"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraSection", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "650ab924-e05c-4914-b7ff-729d8697ee9e"],
 " also extends partial sections."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1c552aa1-3414-4aa9-af65-c66bb4bf5ca5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An exact count ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " larger than the number of continuous sections gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d6f082ef-9a9b-4076-afec-7f70ad5c10cb"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3b1d80e9-95e8-47ca-91a9-980d7b9f98d0"],

Cell["\<\
On a covering of a connected base, a continuous section is a sheet: a copy of \
the base in the total graph. A connected covering has none.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c1864dc1-aa85-4493-b9f8-f9f1cd7b76fd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The number of continuous sections can grow exponentially with the size of \
the base, so ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9db3a215-1820-460f-9af8-7f36b1cc1075"],
 " can be slow."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9923be71-2028-4f8c-a883-024631d70f94"]
}, Open  ]],

